    "interpretation": "Accounting for cohort clustering increases the standard error of the discordance gap by 2.30x (widening the 95% CI from 0.1104 to 0.2440, a 121.0% increase). Despite this expansion, the lower bound (+0.3643) remains far above zero, confirming the discordance thesis is robust."
