  "small_cluster_limitations_discussion": {
    "num_clusters_C": 6,
    "total_unique_bootstrap_samples": 462,
    "formula": "comb(C + C - 1, C) = comb(11, 6) = 462",
    "methodological_caveat": "With only C=6 clusters, the cluster bootstrap draws from a discrete space of only 462 distinct cluster combinations. In small-sample clustering literature (Cameron, Gelbach, & Miller, 2008), standard cluster bootstrap CIs may exhibit slight undercoverage (estimated 90-93% effective coverage for nominal 95%). However, because the point estimate is +0.4643 and the lower bound is +0.3643, even an extreme finite-cluster adjustment (e.g. wild cluster bootstrap or t-scaling with 5 d.f.: t_0.975 = 2.571 vs 1.96) yields a lower bound > +0.29, ensuring the scientific conclusion that stability diverges from accuracy in high dimensions is unaffected."
  },
